#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:3
msgid "Parallel Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:5
msgid ""
"Parallel Agents lets you run multiple agent threads at once, each working "
"independently with its own agent, context window, and conversation history. "
"The Threads Sidebar is where you start, manage, and switch between them."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:7
msgid ""
"Open the Threads Sidebar with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-j\\|ctrl-alt-"
"j</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:9
msgid ""
"**Note:** From version 0.233.0 onward, the Agent Panel and Threads Sidebar "
"are on the left by default. The Project Panel, Git Panel, and other panels "
"move to the right, keeping the thread list and conversation next to each "
"other. To rearrange panels, right-click any panel icon."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:11
msgid "Threads Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:13
msgid ""
"The sidebar shows your threads grouped by project. Each project gets its own "
"section with a header. Threads appear below with their title, status "
"indicator, and which agent is running them. Threads running in linked Git "
"worktrees appear under the same project as their main worktree. See "
"[Worktree Isolation](#worktree-isolation)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:15
msgid ""
"To focus the sidebar without toggling it, use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-"
"alt-;\\|ctrl-alt-;</kbd>. To search your threads, press <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-f\\|ctrl-f</kbd> while the sidebar is focused."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:17
msgid "Switching Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:19
msgid ""
"Click any thread in the sidebar to switch to it. The Agent Panel updates to "
"show that thread's conversation."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:21
msgid ""
"For quick switching without opening the sidebar, use the thread switcher: "
"press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-tab\\|ctrl-tab</kbd> to cycle forward "
"through recent threads, or hold `Shift` while pressing that binding to go "
"backward. This works from both the Agent Panel and the Threads Sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:23
msgid "Thread History"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:25
msgid ""
"To remove a thread from the sidebar, you can archive it by hovering over it "
"and clicking the archive icon that appears. You can also select a thread and "
"press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-backspace\\|shift-backspace</kbd>. "
"Running threads cannot be moved to history until they finish."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:27
msgid ""
"The Thread History view holds all your threads, including ones that you have "
"archived. Toggle it with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-g\\|ctrl-g</kbd> or "
"by clicking the clock icon in the sidebar bottom bar, next to the sidebar "
"toggle."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:29
msgid ""
"To restore a thread, open Thread History and click the thread you want to "
"bring back. Zed moves it back to the thread list and opens it in the Agent "
"Panel. If the thread was running in a Git worktree that was removed, Zed "
"restores the worktree automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:31
msgid ""
"To permanently delete a thread, open Thread History, hover over the thread, "
"and click the trash icon. This removes the thread's conversation history and "
"cleans up any associated worktree data. Deleted threads cannot be recovered."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:33
msgid ""
"You can search your threads in history; search will fuzzy match on thread "
"titles."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:35
msgid "Importing External Agent Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:37
msgid ""
"If you have external agents installed, Zed will detect whether you have "
"existing threads and invite you to import them into Zed. Once you open "
"Thread History, you'll find an import icon button in the Thread History "
"toolbar that lets you import threads at any time. Clicking on it opens a "
"modal where you can select the agents whose threads you want to import."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:39
msgid ""
"**Note:** Thread import is subject to agent support. Some agents (such as "
"Cursor and Gemini CLI) are not currently supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:41
msgid "Running Multiple Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:43
msgid ""
"Each thread runs independently, so you can send a prompt, open a second "
"thread, and give it a different task while the first continues working. To "
"scope a new thread to a specific project, hover over that project's header "
"in the Threads Sidebar and click the `+` button, or use <code "
"class=\"hljs\">agents sidebar: new thread in group</code> from the keyboard. "
"See [Creating New Threads](./agent-panel.md#new-thread) for the other entry "
"points."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:45
msgid ""
"Each thread can use a different agent, so you can run Zed's built-in agent "
"in one thread and an [external agent](./external-agents.md) like Claude Code "
"or Codex in another."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:47
msgid "Multiple Projects"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:49
msgid ""
"The Threads Sidebar can hold multiple projects at once. Each project gets "
"its own group with its own threads and conversation history."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:51
msgid ""
"To add another project to the sidebar, click the **Add Project** button "
"(open-folder icon) in the sidebar bottom bar. The popover that opens lists "
"your recent projects and also provides **Add Local Folders** and **Add "
"Remote Folder** buttons at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:53
msgid "Multi-Root Folder Projects"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:55
msgid ""
"A single project can contain multiple folders (a multi-root folder project). "
"Agents can then read and write across all of those folders in a single "
"thread. There are multiple ways to set one up:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:57
msgid ""
"**From the sidebar:** Click the **Add Project** button, choose **Add Local "
"Folders**, and select multiple folders in the file picker. They open "
"together as one multi-root project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:58
msgid ""
"**From the title bar:** Click the project picker (the leftmost project "
"name). For any local entry in the recent projects list, hover it and click "
"the folder-with-plus icon (**Add Folder to this Project**) to merge that "
"project's folders into the current project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:59
msgid ""
"**From the Project panel:** Right-click a root folder or any empty space in "
"the Project panel and choose **Add Folders to Project** to add more folders "
"to the current project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:61
msgid "Worktree Isolation"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:63
msgid ""
"If two threads might edit the same files, start one in a new Git worktree to "
"give it an isolated checkout."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:65
msgid ""
"Worktrees are managed from the title bar. Click the worktree picker (to the "
"right of the project picker) to switch between existing worktrees or create "
"a new one. New worktrees are created in a detached HEAD state, so you won't "
"accidentally share a branch between worktrees."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:67
msgid ""
"Once you're in a new worktree, use the branch picker next to the worktree "
"picker to create a new branch or check out an existing one. If the branch "
"you pick is already checked out in another worktree, the current worktree "
"stays in detached HEAD until you choose a different branch."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:69
msgid ""
"To automate setup steps whenever a new worktree is created use a [Task hook]"
"(../tasks.md#hooks). The `create_worktree` hook runs automatically after Zed "
"creates a linked worktree, with `ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` pointing at the new "
"worktree and `ZED_MAIN_GIT_WORKTREE` pointing at the original repository."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:71
msgid ""
"After the agent finishes, review the diff and merge the changes through your "
"normal Git workflow. If the thread was running in a linked worktree and no "
"other active threads use it, moving the thread to Thread History saves the "
"worktree's Git state and removes it from disk. Restoring the thread from "
"history restores the worktree."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:73
msgid "See Also"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:75
msgid ""
"[Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md): Manage individual threads and configure the "
"agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:76
msgid ""
"[External Agents](./external-agents.md): Use Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and "
"other agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:77
msgid "[Tools](./tools.md): Built-in tools available in each thread"
msgstr ""
